0.9.0: batteries included - sample photos

Six sample photographs (the author's own, CC BY 4.0) ship in
web/samples/ with a manifest carrying captions and a suggested camera
per photo: a cat portrait for the Polaroids, a driftwood beach and a
deep-sky bell tower for slide film and Autochrome, a Geneva street for
Kodachrome, a fine-detail still life, and a Jaguar Mk2 for the
historical cameras. EXIF orientation is baked at build time; 1600 px
long edge, ~1.8 MB total plus 8-12 KB thumbnails.

The web page gains a click-to-load sample strip under the drop zone;
clicking a sample feeds it through the exact same path as a dropped
file and preselects the suggested camera. Samples deploy to gh-pages
with the rest of web/ and stay untracked on main like the film
library; the tarball carries them for CLI users. Node tests verify the
strip populates and a shipped sample renders through the engine.
